commit 5b38953deb2c0f5bd536314e9dd767160a28864f

C03: a screen reading composes from a bounded excerpt of the recognized lines (SCREEN1415)

SCREEN1413 measured the reviewed screen reading with the lexical checks and the dense budget in place: no draft was vetoed any more, but given the whole recognized text the model transcribed it instead of quoting a few lines; two finals were faithful verbatim excerpts cut at the token cap, five exhausted the budget.

llm._compose_situation_payload: for ocr.read the composer receives an excerpt (the first three lines with real content, each capped at 120 characters, taken from the layout lines because the provider joins the text with spaces), the number of excerpt lines, the total line count and the language; the whole text is no longer in the prompt, so the report is bounded by construction and the grounding check runs against the excerpt.
llm.compose_user_message: the instruction says that seen.text holds a few lines read from the screen and asks to state the total line count and quote those lines verbatim, nothing else.

No .NET change. Offline probe with a real receipt: three lines, a 123-character grounded draft passes, prompt 1.5 K characters. Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


